This product is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see the LICENSE
file). It orchestrates Nextflow (https://www.nextflow.io/, Apache License 2.0)
but does not bundle or redistribute it.

The workflow analysis image (backend/bioflow) installs BioFlow-Insight
(https://gitlab.liris.cnrs.fr/sharefair/bioflow-insight, MIT License) and its
dependencies from PyPI, and the Nextflow language server it bundles
(Apache License 2.0). N-WAVE does not copy their code.

The I/O monitor's image (backend/monitor) builds the eBPF programs of
Witzke et al., "Low-level I/O Monitoring for Scientific Workflows"
(https://github.com/CRC-FONDA/workflow-monitoring), from a pinned commit of
their repository, with the authors' permission, and BCC
(https://github.com/iovisor/bcc, Apache License 2.0). It is built on the
user's computer; N-WAVE patches their code only as backend/monitor/patches
shows.
